# Ruoyi-diancan Auto Sync Rule

After completing **any** user-facing task in workspace `e:\ruoyi-vue3` (bugfix, feature, config, SQL, docs, etc.), the agent MUST automatically:

1. Stage all changes: `git add -A` from `e:\ruoyi-vue3`
2. Commit with a message summarizing the task, in the form:
   `type(scope): summary` — e.g. `fix(dispatch): replace proxy.$modal with direct modal import to fix unresponsive buttons`
3. Push to the **`dev` branch** of the remote:
   `git push -u origin dev` (first push) or `git push origin dev` (subsequent)
4. Report the commit hash + pushed branch in the final reply so the user can review/merge to main manually.

## Remote

- Repo: https://github.com/Frankie222222222222/Ruoyi-diancan.git
- User will merge `dev` → `main` manually. **Never push directly to main.**

## When NOT to push

- The change is purely exploratory (e.g. running `ls`, reading files, no file written)
- The task explicitly says "don't commit" or "只测试一下"
- The build/tests failed — fix them first

## When push FAILS

- If authentication error: STOP and tell the user to set up a Personal Access Token (PAT) or SSH key. Do NOT retry blindly.
- If non-fast-forward: `git pull --rebase origin dev` then push again.
- If conflict: stop and report; never force-push to dev.

## Commit message convention

```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

<body — what & why, not how>
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `refactor`, `docs`, `chore`, `test`, `sql`
Scope: module name (e.g. `dispatch`, `order`, `rider`, `merchant`, `takeout-module`, `frontend`)

## Initialization (one-time, only on first sync)

If `e:\ruoyi-vue3` is not yet a git repo:

```powershell
cd e:\ruoyi-vue3
git init
git checkout -b dev
git remote add origin https://github.com/Frankie222222222222/Ruoyi-diancan.git
# Then ask user for credential setup before first push
```

